    "content": "Lesson 20: Laws of Logarithms \nLearning Outcome(s): At the end of the lesson, the learner is able to illustrate the \nlaws of logarithms. \nLesson Outline: \n1. Laws of logarithms \n2. Change of base formula \n \nLaws of Logarithms.Let b > 0, b \u2260 1 and let n  . For u > 0, v > 0, then \n1. logb(uv) = logbu + logbv \n(Example: log2(3x) = log23 + log2x) \n2. logb(u/v) = logbu \u2013 logbv \n(Example: log3(4/5) = log34 \u2013 log35) \n3. logbun = n\u00b7logbu \n \n(Example: log536 = log562 = 2log56)",
