    "chunk_index": 389,
    "content": "electronic or mechanical including photocopying \u2013 without written permission from the DepEd Central Office. First Edition, 2016.\nDEPED COPY\n112 \n \n3. Applying the one-to-one property of logarithmic functions; \n4. The Zero Factor Property: If ab = 0, then a = 0 or b = 0. \n \nExample 1. Find the value of x in the following equations. \na. log4(2x) = log410 \nSolution. \nlog4(2x) = log410 \n        2x = 10  \n(one-to-one property) \n          x = 5",
