    "lesson": "your lesson here"
  },
  {
    "chunk_index": 756,
    "content": "are associated with virtually every stock market in the world, bond market indices are \nfar less common. In fact, other than certain regional bond indices which have sub-\nindices covering the Philippines, our bond market does not typically compute a bond \nmarket index. Instead, the market rates produced from the bond market are interest \nrates which may be used as benchmarks for other financial instruments. \n \nThe Bond Market and Government Bonds",
    "subject": "General Mathematics",
    "grade": "11",
    "unit": "your unit here",
